@Notes for developers: Use `getlistingstatus` to verify a list by ID
@Note by script writers: use `setlistingstatus` to change the status of a list in this script
USE: This script poses information about a list when double clicking on it. It also has a feature that updates a property of a list editing that property in the GUI, or changing the value of a variable in a block of text.
Right click on any list entry. Choose "Listing details" in the menu that appears. The menu will expand and include a list of listed details. Then you can expand those elements as much as you want to see detailed information. When you start double clicking something to get more information, you will want a "divided window." Do that in the upper left, just above the program icon. That way, you can see all things open on a single screen without having to return to different windows, which is tedious.
